Risks Related To Ownership Of Our Common Stock
Our stock price may be volatile, and you may not be able to resell shares of our common stock at or above the price you paid.
The market price of our common stock could be subject to significant fluctuations. Market prices for securities of early-stage medical device,
pharmaceutical and other life sciences companies have historically been particularly volatile. Some of the factors that may cause the market price of our
common stock to fluctuate include:
• a slowdown in the medical device industry or the general economy;
• inability to obtain adequate supply of the components for any of our products, or inability to do so at acceptable prices;
• performance of third parties on whom the we may rely, including for the manufacture of the components for our product, including their ability to
comply with regulatory requirements;
• the results of our current and any future clinical trials of our devices;
